{
  "name": "enantiornithine",
  "description": "Adult enantiornithine ('opposite bird'), Cretaceous, standing facing right with wings half-raised: brown-grey #6a5a4a feathers, paler belly, long snout open a crack with a row of small sharp white teeth top and bottom, a hooked claw on the leading edge of each wing, long legs with hooked talons, small hard yellow eye under a heavy brow, short fan tail. Menacing, not cute. Teeth and wing claws stick out of the outline so they read in silhouette. Bottom-centre anchor (feet on y=0), ~420x300.",
